{% doc %}
  A row of product cards that scrolls sideways, with arrows — the pattern on
  us.thehoffbrand.com: the cards sit on one scroll track with snap points, the
  scrollbar is hidden, and two arrows at the right of the heading move it by a
  screenful at a time. The track is a plain scroll container, so a trackpad, a
  touch swipe and the keyboard all work whether or not the arrows are there;
  the arrows are an addition, never the only way through (they are hidden
  outright on phones, where swiping is the natural gesture).

  @param {string} strip_id - unique id, used to tie the arrows to the track
  @param {string} cards - the already-rendered <li> cards, in order. Captured
    by the caller (as Related products does) because Liquid cannot build an
    array of products one at a time: `concat` only joins two arrays.
  @param {string} [heading] - shown at the left of the arrow row
  @example
  {% render 'product-strip', strip_id: section.id, cards: cards, heading: 'You may like' %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign prev_label = 'general.strip.previous' | t
  assign next_label = 'general.strip.next' | t
-%}

{%- if cards contains 'product-card' or cards contains 'image-card' -%}
  <div class="product-strip" data-product-strip>
    <div class="product-strip__head">
      {%- if heading != blank -%}
        <h2 class="product-strip__heading">{{ heading }}</h2>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        Hidden until theme.js has measured that the track really does overflow
        — arrows that cannot move anything are worse than no arrows.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="product-strip__arrows" data-strip-arrows hidden>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="product-strip__arrow"
          data-strip-prev
          aria-controls="ProductStrip-{{ strip_id }}"
          aria-label="{{ prev_label }}"
        >
          <svg class="product-strip__chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <path d="M15 4 L7 12 L15 20" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" />
          </svg>
        </button>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="product-strip__arrow"
          data-strip-next
          aria-controls="ProductStrip-{{ strip_id }}"
          aria-label="{{ next_label }}"
        >
          <svg class="product-strip__chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <path d="M9 4 L17 12 L9 20" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" />
          </svg>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      tabindex makes the scroll area reachable by keyboard: a region that
      scrolls has to be operable without a mouse (WCAG 2.1.1), and browsers
      only hand focus to such a container on their own in some engines.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <ul
      class="product-strip__track"
      id="ProductStrip-{{ strip_id }}"
      data-strip-track
      tabindex="0"
      role="list"
      aria-label="{{ heading | default: next_label | escape }}"
    >
      {{ cards }}
    </ul>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
